WEBVTT

00:00:00.601 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.766 --> 00:00:05.550
In this lesson, we blow-dry long, layered hair:

00:00:05.725 --> 00:00:10.830
smooth, shiny, with a little volume at the roots, and softly curved ends.

00:00:11.259 --> 00:00:13.790
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:14.088 --> 00:00:15.070
Here, we do it.

00:00:15.661 --> 00:00:16.362
Step one:

00:00:16.545 --> 00:00:17.322
preparation.

00:00:17.852 --> 00:00:18.697
Round brushes,

00:00:18.647 --> 00:00:22.842
a paddle brush and clips have all been cleaned after the previous client.

00:00:23.186 --> 00:00:24.122
Check the dryer:

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:29.322
the nozzle firmly attached, the filter clean, and the cord not kinked or cracked.

00:00:29.793 --> 00:00:33.642
Raise the chair to the right height, so your elbows stay below your shoulders.

00:00:34.236 --> 00:00:35.021
Step two:

00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:37.021
towel-dry and detangle.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:42.220
Wrap the hair in a towel, and press gently from root to ends, without rubbing.

00:00:42.968 --> 00:00:46.018
Detangle with a wide-tooth comb, starting at the ends,

00:00:45.968 --> 00:00:48.461
with your other hand holding the hair above.

00:00:49.145 --> 00:00:49.997
Step three:

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:51.197
heat protection.

00:00:51.645 --> 00:00:55.383
Spray it evenly over the mid-lengths and ends, from a little distance,

00:00:55.333 --> 00:00:57.437
using the amount the product instructs.

00:00:57.939 --> 00:01:00.397
The ends are the weakest part, so don't miss them.

00:01:00.810 --> 00:01:03.917
Comb through once more, so the product is spread evenly.

00:01:04.323 --> 00:01:06.077
Spray away from the client's face.

00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:10.245
Colored, bleached, or fine hair needs heat protection even more,

00:01:10.195 --> 00:01:12.077
and an even lower heat setting.

00:01:12.766 --> 00:01:13.618
Step four:

00:01:13.798 --> 00:01:14.498
rough-dry.

00:01:14.763 --> 00:01:15.618
No brush yet.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:19.035
Hold the dryer in one hand, nozzle pointing down,

00:01:18.985 --> 00:01:21.138
about a hand's width from the hair.

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:25.858
Your other hand runs through the roots, lifting gently, and shaking the hair.

00:01:26.444 --> 00:01:29.778
Dry the roots first, because that is where the hair dries slowest.

00:01:30.107 --> 00:01:31.218
Keep the dryer moving.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.818
Dry until the hair is about seventy to eighty percent dry:

00:01:35.084 --> 00:01:37.538
slightly damp to the touch, no longer wet.

00:01:37.785 --> 00:01:39.378
How do you know it is dry enough?

00:01:39.552 --> 00:01:42.895
Slide your hand into the roots at the nape and behind the ears,

00:01:42.845 --> 00:01:44.098
where it dries slowest.

00:01:44.543 --> 00:01:47.218
If it feels cool and wet, it is not ready.

00:01:47.647 --> 00:01:51.538
If it feels slightly damp, and the hair is light and loose, it is ready.

00:01:52.203 --> 00:01:53.148
Step five:

00:01:53.264 --> 00:01:53.948
sectioning.

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:57.201
Clip all the upper hair up on top of the head,

00:01:57.151 --> 00:02:00.508
leaving only a thin layer at the nape, as wide as the brush.

00:02:00.991 --> 00:02:04.828
Clean sections mean faster drying, and no missed pieces.

00:02:05.239 --> 00:02:08.645
With thick hair, take sections thinner than the width of the brush,

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.348
so the air gets through all of it.

00:02:11.020 --> 00:02:11.963
Step six:

00:02:12.143 --> 00:02:13.483
dry the lower layer.

00:02:13.816 --> 00:02:17.083
Place the round brush under a section, close to the roots.

00:02:17.432 --> 00:02:21.883
The nozzle sits parallel to the brush, pointing down, a few centimeters away.

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:26.030
Draw the brush slowly down to the ends, keeping even tension,

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.043
with the dryer following the brush.

00:02:28.472 --> 00:02:32.443
Repeat a few times, until the section is completely dry and shiny.

00:02:32.592 --> 00:02:36.923
At the ends, turn the brush inward a little, so the ends curve softly.

00:02:37.232 --> 00:02:40.405
If the client wants it really straight, with little volume,

00:02:40.355 --> 00:02:42.523
swap the round brush for a paddle brush.

00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:46.574
Brush from root to ends, with the dryer following above the brush,

00:02:46.524 --> 00:02:48.523
and the nozzle still pointing down.

00:02:49.123 --> 00:02:49.973
Step seven:

00:02:50.232 --> 00:02:51.093
cool air.

00:02:51.602 --> 00:02:54.453
The section you have just dried is still wrapped on the brush:

00:02:54.562 --> 00:02:55.333
hold it still.

00:02:55.761 --> 00:02:58.053
Press the cool shot button for a few seconds.

00:02:58.412 --> 00:03:01.813
Only when the hair has cooled, slide the brush out gently.

00:03:02.244 --> 00:03:06.613
Then let down the next layer, and do exactly the same, working gradually up.

00:03:07.258 --> 00:03:08.056
Step eight:

00:03:08.299 --> 00:03:10.696
the sides, and the hair around the face.

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:15.096
Dry section by section, pulling the hair back, away from the face.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.776
Turn the ends outward, so the hair opens up the face.

00:03:19.205 --> 00:03:23.804
For the pieces around the face, place the round brush on the inside of the section,

00:03:23.754 --> 00:03:26.216
close to the face but not touching the skin,

00:03:26.565 --> 00:03:29.176
then dry while turning the brush outward and back.

00:03:29.312 --> 00:03:32.856
The piece will curve out softly, and won't fall into the eyes.

00:03:33.025 --> 00:03:35.191
Near the ears and the nape, go gently,

00:03:35.141 --> 00:03:37.976
and keep the dryer a little further from the skin.

00:03:38.306 --> 00:03:41.416
Cover the client's ear with your hand when drying right next to it.

00:03:41.730 --> 00:03:42.616
Ask the client:

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:43.896
is it too hot?

00:03:44.238 --> 00:03:48.616
When this side is done, move to the other, and compare both sides in the mirror:

00:03:48.969 --> 00:03:52.056
the volume, and the curve at the ends, must match.

00:03:52.793 --> 00:03:53.675
Step nine:

00:03:53.845 --> 00:03:55.355
the top, for volume.

00:03:55.756 --> 00:03:59.435
Take a section at the top, and lift it up high, almost straight up.

00:03:59.945 --> 00:04:02.315
Place the round brush close to the roots.

00:04:02.491 --> 00:04:06.497
Dry the roots first, with the nozzle still pointing down along the hair,

00:04:06.447 --> 00:04:08.475
then draw the brush out to the ends.

00:04:08.888 --> 00:04:11.435
Press the cool shot, and only then release.

00:04:11.678 --> 00:04:15.197
At the parting, dry it to the left and to the right a few times,

00:04:15.147 --> 00:04:16.715
so the roots don't lie flat.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:21.597
If the client wants even more volume, after the cool shot, roll the section up,

00:04:21.547 --> 00:04:23.515
clip it lightly against the head,

00:04:23.711 --> 00:04:27.045
wait until it is completely cool, then remove the clip,

00:04:26.995 --> 00:04:29.195
and smooth it gently with your hand.

00:04:29.791 --> 00:04:31.921
A few common mistakes to watch out for.

00:04:32.315 --> 00:04:35.601
The nozzle pointing upward, from the ends toward the roots:

00:04:35.708 --> 00:04:36.641
instant frizz.

00:04:37.054 --> 00:04:39.361
Holding the dryer on one spot for too long:

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:42.161
the hair gets scorched, and the scalp burns.

00:04:42.498 --> 00:04:43.681
Sections too thick:

00:04:44.032 --> 00:04:48.561
dry on the outside, still damp inside, and the shape drops within an hour.

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:52.001
And when hair gets tangled in a round brush, don't yank it.

00:04:52.335 --> 00:04:56.881
Switch off the dryer, turn the brush back slowly, and untangle it bit by bit.

00:04:57.448 --> 00:05:02.081
If the client has a fringe, dry the fringe first, right after towel-drying,

00:05:02.031 --> 00:05:04.098
because a fringe dries very fast.

00:05:04.545 --> 00:05:08.978
Nozzle pointing down, comb it left, then right, as in the fringe lesson.

00:05:09.623 --> 00:05:10.437
Step ten:

00:05:10.686 --> 00:05:11.397
the finish.

00:05:11.726 --> 00:05:12.677
Check with your hand:

00:05:12.848 --> 00:05:16.277
the hair is completely dry, at the roots and the nape too.

00:05:16.724 --> 00:05:18.917
If it is still damp, the shape will drop.

00:05:19.267 --> 00:05:23.704
Apply a tiny amount of hair oil, or serum, to the ends, very little,

00:05:23.654 --> 00:05:25.317
as the product instructs.

00:05:25.744 --> 00:05:30.037
Show the client how to blow-dry at home, with the dryer and the brush she has.

00:05:30.276 --> 00:05:33.255
Then show her the result, from the front and both sides,

00:05:33.205 --> 00:05:35.557
and ask if she would like anything adjusted.

00:05:35.976 --> 00:05:37.317
Write it in the client record:

00:05:37.574 --> 00:05:41.877
which brush, which product, and whether she prefers volume or sleek.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.597
Next time, whoever blow-dries will know.

00:05:45.260 --> 00:05:46.608
After the client leaves:

00:05:46.638 --> 00:05:49.044
remove the hair from the brushes, wash them,

00:05:48.994 --> 00:05:53.327
and disinfect them as the product instructs, as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:05:53.747 --> 00:05:57.328
Unplug the dryer, let it cool, and only then put it away.

00:05:57.670 --> 00:06:00.528
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
